course: dictionary
lesson: 3977
title: Gaily: happy, bright or careless
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Gaily is one of them. «The children sang gaily.» Children singing is a happy thing, so gaily means in a happy, cheerful, lively way.
explain: «Gaily painted boats» is about colour, not mood. Bright paint makes the boats look cheerful, so here gaily means brightly and colourfully. Ask yourself which meaning fits the picture in your head.
explain: In «He gaily spent all the money», gaily means carelessly, without thinking about the trouble it causes. The clue is that spending all the money is a problem, so the word is not describing happiness here. Always check whether your meaning makes sense in the story.
fact: Gaily is an adverb: it tells you how something is done, such as how the children sang.
fact: «Gaily» means in a happy, cheerful, lively way.
fact: «Gaily» can also mean brightly and colourfully, as in «gaily painted boats».
fact: «Gaily» can mean carelessly, without thinking about the trouble it causes.
fact: In The Wind in the Willows, the weasels sing «Toad he went a-pleasuring / Gaily down the street—», where a-pleasuring means going out for fun.
exercise: «The children sang gaily.» What does gaily mean here? | Without any words | Very quietly and sadly | In a hurry, running fast | *In a happy, cheerful, lively way
exercise: «The gaily painted boats bobbed on the river.» What does gaily tell you about the boats? | They were sinking | *They were brightly and colourfully painted | They were very old and grey | They were made of stone
exercise: «He gaily spent all the money.» What does gaily suggest about the way he spent it? | Sadly, because he was poor | Slowly, counting each coin | *Carelessly, without thinking about the trouble it caused | Carefully, saving every penny
test: «The gaily painted caravan stood by the river.» Which meaning of gaily fits here? | Slowly | Carelessly | *Brightly and colourfully | Sadly
test: Which word is closest in meaning to gaily when it means happy and cheerful? | Quietly | Sadly | Slowly | *Merrily
exam: Mia says gaily always means happy. Is she right? | No, it always means sad | Yes, always | *No, gaily can also mean brightly coloured or carelessly | Yes, but only in songs
